INT. GOLDEN TIGER KARAOKE - PRIVATE ROOM 4 - NIGHT

Velvet booths. A neon tiger glows on the wall. A screen shows lyrics to a song nobody is singing. On the table: a bucket of ice, a tray of cheap whiskey, and a leather briefcase.

MINH-ANH LE, 30s, black dress, sits very still and watches the door. DUKE FONTENOT, 50s, linen jacket, rotates a microphone in his hands like a cigar. TANYA FROST, 40s, beside him, shuffles a deck of cards without looking at them. INES CALDERÓN, 20s, the room's waitress, hovers with a tray and a wary smile.

A MAN IN A LEATHER COAT, 50s, comes in without knocking. He shuts the door gently behind him.

MAN IN LEATHER COAT
Evening, all.

DUKE
You're early.

MAN IN LEATHER COAT
You're late.

He drops into the booth. Takes a glass off Ines's tray and drinks it in one pull. She lowers the tray and backs toward the door.

TANYA
Stay, honey.

INES
I should refill the ice.

TANYA
We have ice.

Ines freezes. Minh-Anh doesn't blink.

MINH-ANH
So. The briefcase.

MAN IN LEATHER COAT
What about it?

MINH-ANH
Open it.

He doesn't move. Duke sets down the microphone.

DUKE
Casimir.

CASIMIR
(slowly)
There it is.

DUKE
Don't be dramatic.

CASIMIR
You said my name like a bad word.

DUKE
It is a bad word, Casimir.

Tanya's cards stop. Minh-Anh's hand drifts to her purse.

CASIMIR (CONT'D)
Ines, sweetheart, put on a song.

INES
Sir?

CASIMIR
Anything. Something loud.

She taps the screen. A power ballad erupts, drums and strings.

Casimir stands. Reaches into his coat. Duke lunges. Minh-Anh rolls over the table. Tanya slams the briefcase shut. In three seconds the booth is a knot of elbows, glass shattering, whiskey flying.

The song soars on.

A pistol clatters to the floor. Everybody stops. Everybody looks at it.

INES
(very small)
That's not my ice.
